WEBVTT

00:08.690 --> 00:16.160
aozameta machinami yureru boku no kage

00:08.690 --> 00:16.160
The pale street, my swaying shadow,

00:16.160 --> 00:24.440
nibui ashidori wa yuku saki wo shirazu

00:16.160 --> 00:24.440
I walk slowly, not knowing my destination.

00:24.440 --> 00:30.480
kawasenu omoi

00:24.440 --> 00:30.480
My feelings can't reach yours.

00:31.240 --> 00:38.620
kimi no hitomi no naka utsushidasu mono wo

00:31.240 --> 00:38.620
The things reflected in the depths of your eyes,

00:38.620 --> 00:46.860
uketomeru tame ni hashiridashiteita

00:38.620 --> 00:46.860
I started running in order to catch up to them.

00:46.860 --> 01:00.640
sashidasu sono te wo hodokerai youni nigirikaesu

00:46.860 --> 01:00.640
I grip your outstretched hand without letting go.

01:01.170 --> 01:08.680
hanbun no tsuki no yoru wa bokura wo terashite

01:01.170 --> 01:08.680
On this night, the half moon shines upon us.

01:08.680 --> 01:15.990
oikaketekita jikan wo boku wa furikitte

01:08.680 --> 01:15.990
I shake off the flow of time chasing after us.

01:16.220 --> 01:27.430
hanbun zutsu no bokura wa egaku saki made mo mieru

01:16.220 --> 01:27.430
We're half of ourselves, but we can draw the future.

01:30.540 --> 01:32.000
What do you mean?

01:32.500 --> 01:34.370
Did the operation fail?

01:34.640 --> 01:36.370
No, it went well.

01:37.040 --> 01:38.510
Everything that could be done was done.

01:38.980 --> 01:41.580
Even if we do it again, it won't go as smooth as this one.

01:41.580 --> 01:42.710
Does that mean...

01:42.710 --> 01:44.380
it's a success?

01:44.380 --> 01:45.520
Probably.

01:45.520 --> 01:48.890
We'll observe her for the next two days and if nothing happens, then it can count as a success.

01:49.190 --> 01:51.590
Then, what do you mean by that?

01:51.590 --> 01:53.520
Why is it the worst?

01:53.520 --> 01:55.190
You'll know soon.

01:55.190 --> 01:57.030
Whether you want to know or not.

01:57.660 --> 02:02.630
Our Hands Will

02:03.530 --> 02:06.000
Note: ICU stands for "Intensive Care Unit"

02:06.570 --> 02:07.510
Akiko-san.

02:07.510 --> 02:09.610
You scared me there.

02:10.310 --> 02:11.940
Umm, how's Rika?

02:13.440 --> 02:15.810
Well, everything looks normal.

02:15.810 --> 02:17.020
I see.

02:17.020 --> 02:18.050
Then, let's go.

02:18.050 --> 02:21.490
Not even I have the means to sneak you into ICU.

02:21.490 --> 02:22.520
Okay.

02:27.190 --> 02:28.730
Hey, Yuuichi.

02:28.730 --> 02:30.090
What is it?

02:30.090 --> 02:31.000
About that...

02:32.830 --> 02:34.000
It's nothing.

02:35.470 --> 02:38.040
Anyway, have you been studying?

02:38.040 --> 02:39.670
Ah, not at all.

02:39.670 --> 02:41.740
If you don't study hard, you'll have to redo a grade.

02:41.740 --> 02:43.140
Rika is working hard right now too.

02:43.140 --> 02:44.480
You'd better work hard too.

02:46.440 --> 02:49.310
What I just said, did it sound like something a nurse would say?

02:51.450 --> 02:53.580
Children today, honestly...

02:53.580 --> 02:56.250
Why can't you just say "I'll work hard"?

02:57.190 --> 02:58.560
What are you doing?

03:00.260 --> 03:02.690
Okay, hurry back to your room.

03:02.690 --> 03:03.960
Yeah, yeah.

03:09.900 --> 03:10.840
Yuuichi?

03:12.500 --> 03:14.440
Do you know yet?

03:14.440 --> 03:15.370
Eh?

03:15.370 --> 03:16.570
About what?

03:19.210 --> 03:21.850
Hurry up and go back, brat.

03:45.800 --> 03:46.600
Umm...

03:46.600 --> 03:49.610
What are you planning to do after you graduate from high school?

03:49.610 --> 03:50.310
Huh?

03:51.080 --> 03:52.410
Are you going to university?

03:52.980 --> 03:53.710
Yeah.

03:54.410 --> 03:57.680
In Tokyo or Nagoya?

03:57.680 --> 03:58.550
Yeah.

03:58.550 --> 03:59.950
Probably.

03:59.950 --> 04:01.650
You want to leave Ise?

04:01.650 --> 04:02.720
Yeah.

04:02.720 --> 04:03.590
I see.

04:06.020 --> 04:06.620
Well...

04:06.620 --> 04:07.590
Good luck.

04:09.190 --> 04:10.130
Umm...

04:10.860 --> 04:11.600
Huh?

04:12.230 --> 04:14.330
Will Rika get better?

04:15.470 --> 04:16.570
What do you mean?

04:16.570 --> 04:19.440
So she can go out...

04:19.440 --> 04:21.870
and return to her normal life.

04:23.570 --> 04:25.510
That's none of your business.

04:25.780 --> 04:26.440
Huh?

04:27.880 --> 04:30.550
I know you have a good relationship with Rika,

04:30.550 --> 04:32.950
but please don't misunderstand.

04:35.650 --> 04:38.360
You're not part of Rika's family.

04:38.360 --> 04:39.720
Just one of her close friends.

04:40.260 --> 04:42.590
As her chief physician, I have a duty to keep it confidential.

04:43.460 --> 04:46.200
I can't just tell anyone about the condition of the patient.

04:47.830 --> 04:48.670
Umm...

04:49.770 --> 04:51.500
Is there something else?

04:51.500 --> 04:52.600
Uh...

04:52.600 --> 04:54.210
Why did you say this is the worst outcome?

04:55.610 --> 04:56.840
What does it mean?

04:59.110 --> 05:01.450
Because you will always be here.

05:01.780 --> 05:02.580
Huh?

05:03.820 --> 05:05.450
Later then, brat.

05:15.190 --> 05:17.530
What do you plan to do, doctor?

05:17.530 --> 05:18.430
About what?

05:18.430 --> 05:21.370
Do you plan not to tell Yuuichi the truth about Rika's condition?

05:21.370 --> 05:22.930
That is against confidentiality.

05:24.440 --> 05:27.970
That idiot may be stupid, but he must have noticed it too.

05:27.970 --> 05:30.140
Everytime I see him, he looks like he's about to cry.

05:30.140 --> 05:32.040
He doesn't even have the power to pretend to act tough.

05:32.480 --> 05:33.540
I see.

05:35.180 --> 05:37.180
Can't you make an exception?

05:37.180 --> 05:38.080
Impossible.

05:38.080 --> 05:41.220
You're not afraid that I tell everyone about you drinking during your shift?

05:41.220 --> 05:42.250
Go right ahead.

05:42.250 --> 05:45.020
You're not afraid that I tell everyone that you beat up a patient?

05:45.290 --> 05:46.520
Go right ahead.

05:46.890 --> 05:48.630
If people found out, you'd be fired.

05:49.190 --> 05:51.230
Then my life would probably be a lot happier.

05:52.960 --> 05:54.900
Damn you! Don't try to act tough!

05:54.900 --> 05:57.570
Why can't you think from their perspective?

05:58.140 --> 05:59.300
For Ezaki...

05:59.840 --> 06:01.670
It's better for him not to know.

06:02.670 --> 06:06.840
Besides, the situation is different now.

06:08.110 --> 06:10.950
Rika's mother made a request.

06:14.090 --> 06:15.250
Take a seat.

06:18.990 --> 06:22.160
Rika will leave ICU today and return to her room.

06:22.160 --> 06:26.060
Her condition has stabilized and will be observed in her room from now on.

06:28.470 --> 06:29.870
And...

06:31.300 --> 06:32.540
Ezaki...

06:32.540 --> 06:33.810
This is a warning.

06:34.270 --> 06:36.810
You are not allowed to go over to the East Wing from now on.

06:38.480 --> 06:44.320
You brought a patient who could've had a relapse at anytime out without permission.

06:44.920 --> 06:46.990
To tell you the truth...

06:46.990 --> 06:48.150
It's troublesome for us too.

06:48.490 --> 06:50.320
Rika's mother is very angry about this too.

06:50.960 --> 06:51.820
Her mother...

06:52.290 --> 06:54.060
Let me repeat it again.

06:54.060 --> 06:56.560
You're not part of Rika's family.

06:56.890 --> 06:58.160
To her, you're just an outsider.

06:59.360 --> 07:01.570
You are not allowed to go over to the East Wing from now on.

07:02.030 --> 07:05.500
If you don't heed to this warning, you'll be forced out of the hospital immediately.

07:10.440 --> 07:11.240
That's it.

07:11.240 --> 07:12.080
Go back.

07:14.250 --> 07:15.710
Go back, Yuuichi.

07:15.710 --> 07:16.410
Okay.

07:16.910 --> 07:18.120
Stand up.

07:18.120 --> 07:19.080
Okay.

07:19.080 --> 07:19.950
Let's go.

07:20.450 --> 07:21.190
Okay.

07:24.720 --> 07:26.860
Hey, your hand stopped.

07:28.560 --> 07:30.800
If you don't hurry, you won't be able to finish.

07:32.260 --> 07:33.970
Though I don't mind.

07:33.970 --> 07:36.030
You are the one who'll need to redo a grade.

07:39.770 --> 07:40.810
How did it go?

07:41.440 --> 07:43.780
Was that girl's operation successful?

07:44.880 --> 07:45.840
Probably.

07:45.840 --> 07:46.910
What do you mean?

07:46.910 --> 07:48.480
I can't help it!

07:48.480 --> 07:49.550
I don't know either.

07:51.650 --> 07:52.850
I'm disappointed.

07:53.890 --> 07:55.820
You haven't gone to visit her?

07:55.820 --> 07:57.790
Isn't now the most important time for her recovery?

07:57.790 --> 07:58.660
Yuu-chan,

07:58.660 --> 08:01.090
why did you go through all that trouble at school?

08:01.090 --> 08:01.890
Shut up!

08:42.330 --> 08:43.570
Oh, Ezaki.

08:44.500 --> 08:46.170
What are you doing here?

08:46.170 --> 08:47.810
Waiting for you.

08:48.270 --> 08:49.070
Huh?

08:58.680 --> 09:00.350
What? Still awake?

09:00.350 --> 09:01.250
I guess.

09:03.390 --> 09:04.560
You're not going to sleep?

09:06.290 --> 09:06.920
How annoying.

09:06.920 --> 09:08.060
Stop it.

09:08.060 --> 09:08.830
Ah...

09:09.560 --> 09:10.660
Stop it!

09:13.200 --> 09:14.530
What is it?

09:15.230 --> 09:18.100
I told a lie.

09:18.100 --> 09:18.970
A lie?

09:19.240 --> 09:23.470
I told Ezaki something not even I can believe.

09:29.450 --> 09:31.850
My hands...

09:33.520 --> 09:34.650
Hey, Tanizaki...

09:34.650 --> 09:36.320
Let me tell you an old story.

09:36.690 --> 09:38.490
An old story?

09:38.490 --> 09:39.960
My friend's...

09:39.960 --> 09:42.330
boring, old story.

09:43.530 --> 09:45.300
Fine, I'll listen.

09:46.100 --> 09:47.900
That guy was in the same year as I.

09:47.900 --> 09:49.670
He entered the number one medical school,

09:49.670 --> 09:51.570
became a number one doctor,

09:51.570 --> 09:54.240
and was planning on having a number one life.

09:57.810 --> 10:01.110
He used to have a really cute girlfriend.

10:01.110 --> 10:03.250
Even though she can't be compared to those idols...

10:03.250 --> 10:05.150
She's an innocent and honest girl.

10:06.780 --> 10:09.290
The two got married when he was still in medical school.

10:09.290 --> 10:12.590
Even though they weren't rich, their lives were filled with happiness.

10:13.220 --> 10:16.360
They both believed that they'd be happy forever.

10:17.630 --> 10:19.060
Until that day...

10:20.230 --> 10:22.770
Dilated cardiomyopathy.

10:24.100 --> 10:27.370
His girlfriend's heart held an unpredictable time bomb.

10:30.510 --> 10:32.440
She was diagnosed with cardiac insufficiency...

10:32.440 --> 10:34.750
and was saved with an operation.

10:35.410 --> 10:37.580
The five-year survival rate is only 50%.

10:37.580 --> 10:39.250
Out of every two patients, one will die.

10:39.750 --> 10:42.250
Even if the illness is under control, she'll never be able to fully recover...

10:42.550 --> 10:45.690
And even if she can somehow hold on,
she won't have long to live...

10:45.690 --> 10:46.890
Isn't that...

10:47.290 --> 10:49.760
Yeah, it's like Rika's condition right now.

10:52.130 --> 10:55.000
I don't know if it's because of his ability or his luck...

10:55.470 --> 10:58.870
He had a lot of promotion opportunities.

10:58.870 --> 11:02.310
But if he wanted to be one of the elite, she'd become a burden.

11:03.610 --> 11:08.980
He had to set his life and the time he could stay by her side on a balance, and choose.

11:09.310 --> 11:12.520
Even if he chose her, she wouldn't have long to live.

11:12.920 --> 11:14.020
Honestly the worst possible outcome.

11:16.250 --> 11:18.890
This is probably the worst outcome for you.

11:22.760 --> 11:24.200
Is anyone there?

11:39.640 --> 11:40.780
Damn it!

11:40.780 --> 11:42.150
Why is it like this?

11:42.150 --> 11:43.350
Why did it turn out like this?!

11:44.420 --> 11:46.350
Because you'll always be here.

11:46.820 --> 11:48.290
So you're saying...

11:48.290 --> 11:50.960
it'd be better if I'd never met Rika?

12:06.900 --> 12:08.310
"At the risk of my life...

12:08.310 --> 12:09.810
I'll become yours completely."

12:18.780 --> 12:20.890
Tsukasa, please come back me up a bit.

12:26.220 --> 12:27.690
You'd better not break it.

12:27.690 --> 12:29.660
I took it out without my dad's permission.

12:30.330 --> 12:31.160
Thank you.

12:32.400 --> 12:34.370
What are you going to do, Yuu-chan?

12:34.370 --> 12:36.530
Hang down from that water tower,

12:36.530 --> 12:38.240
and get to Rika's room from the outside.

12:40.540 --> 12:42.710
Why don't you use the door to get in?

12:42.710 --> 12:44.640
Her mom won't let me in.

12:44.640 --> 12:46.810
I'll be forced out of the hospital and never see her again.

12:46.810 --> 12:49.450
Can you not go from the opposite roof?

12:49.450 --> 12:52.320
The East Wing's roof is always locked.

12:52.320 --> 12:53.650
It's dangerous!

12:53.650 --> 12:54.590
I'm going to do it!

12:54.590 --> 12:55.990
Definitely going to do it!

12:55.990 --> 12:57.260
Rika has already...

12:57.260 --> 12:59.160
We've run out of time.

12:59.160 --> 12:59.890
But...

12:59.890 --> 13:01.160
Mizutani!

13:01.930 --> 13:02.930
Let it go.

13:02.930 --> 13:04.660
Let Ezaki do what he thinks is right.

13:04.930 --> 13:07.630
I agree with Yamanishi-kun.

13:10.000 --> 13:12.770
Why do you always have to wear that zebra mask?

13:12.770 --> 13:13.640
Ah, because...

13:13.640 --> 13:17.040
One of my relatives is working here as a nurse. It'd be bad if I was discovered.

13:25.420 --> 13:26.380
Here I come!

13:39.800 --> 13:42.270
Rika, I'll be right there!

13:52.280 --> 13:53.310
Good luck!

13:53.310 --> 13:54.080
Yuu-chan!

13:54.310 --> 13:55.480
Yuuichi!

14:01.420 --> 14:02.320
Ezaki!

14:03.150 --> 14:04.960
Damn it!

14:07.530 --> 14:09.630
Just a little more, Yuuichi!

14:16.930 --> 14:18.100
Yuu-chan!

14:24.810 --> 14:26.640
Th-This is bad, Sekoguchi!

14:26.640 --> 14:30.150
Yamanishi-kun, there's a cell phone in my pocket.

14:30.150 --> 14:32.180
Can you call someone for me?

14:32.180 --> 14:34.490
This isn't the time to call!

14:39.620 --> 14:41.430
Is it impossible after all?

14:42.330 --> 14:43.930
How embarrassing...

14:44.630 --> 14:45.660
Kid.

14:47.400 --> 14:49.230
Ta... Tada-san?

14:49.800 --> 14:51.770
What happened, kid?

14:51.770 --> 14:54.210
Having such a tired expression on your face...

14:54.610 --> 14:56.640
Tada-san... I...

14:57.080 --> 14:59.210
When the girl you like appears...

14:59.210 --> 15:01.080
You have to declare your feelings loudly!

15:04.950 --> 15:06.150
Yuuichi!

15:06.150 --> 15:09.890
One day, you'll meet a girl you like too.

15:09.890 --> 15:10.860
Dad?

15:11.560 --> 15:12.390
Remember.

15:12.390 --> 15:14.160
You have to cherish her!

15:16.290 --> 15:17.600
Oh, Ezaki.

15:18.000 --> 15:19.530
What are you doing?

15:19.530 --> 15:21.430
Waiting for you.

15:21.430 --> 15:22.300
Huh?

15:23.700 --> 15:29.370
You probably think that fate and the future are all pre-determined.

15:31.510 --> 15:35.050
All those are up to you.

15:35.050 --> 15:37.080
Whichever it is, no matter how harsh they are...

15:37.080 --> 15:39.050
You won't be able to escape it.

15:39.420 --> 15:43.520
We have to endure our harsh life in this harsh world.

15:43.960 --> 15:47.090
If fate and the future don't agree with you,

15:47.090 --> 15:48.690
you can deny them,

15:48.690 --> 15:49.960
twist them.

15:49.960 --> 15:51.260
Maybe you can do it,

15:51.260 --> 15:52.760
maybe you can't.

15:53.300 --> 15:56.300
But even if there's only a 1% chance, you can't give up!

15:57.040 --> 15:58.040
Do you understand?

15:58.040 --> 15:59.400
Huh?

15:59.400 --> 16:02.410
For Rika's sake, you can do anything, right?

16:03.370 --> 16:05.340
If there's something you really long for,

16:05.340 --> 16:06.610
you have to reach for it.

16:06.610 --> 16:09.050
That's exactly what your hands are there for.

16:15.990 --> 16:18.720
My hands...

16:24.430 --> 16:25.760
One more time!

16:25.760 --> 16:27.030
Pull me up!

16:27.030 --> 16:29.530
It's impossible. Forget about it!

16:29.530 --> 16:30.500
I can't!

16:30.500 --> 16:32.170
This isn't just about me!

16:32.470 --> 16:34.070
Rika is waiting for me!

16:34.070 --> 16:35.970
I'm going there no matter what happens!

16:35.970 --> 16:38.680
Alright, let me lend you my strength.

16:41.550 --> 16:43.450
Zebra mask the second?

16:43.450 --> 16:45.250
Ah, that's my brother.

16:45.250 --> 16:46.050
Huh?

16:54.060 --> 16:55.160
He did it!

16:55.160 --> 16:56.430
Yuu-chan!

17:20.120 --> 17:21.350
You are...

17:21.350 --> 17:22.290
Please open up!

17:22.590 --> 17:24.720
Just what do you intend to do?

17:23.690 --> 17:24.720
I'm begging you!

17:24.720 --> 17:25.890
Please open up!

17:27.160 --> 17:29.830
You should stop messing around.

17:29.830 --> 17:31.730
Breaking in from the window in the middle of the night...

17:31.730 --> 17:32.860
Do you have any common sense?

17:32.860 --> 17:34.630
Please let me talk to Rika.

17:35.400 --> 17:37.200
I understand that what I'm doing is out of line.

17:37.200 --> 17:38.900
But I just want to talk to her.

17:38.900 --> 17:40.040
I won't allow that.

17:40.410 --> 17:41.570
I'm begging you!

17:42.110 --> 17:43.070
It's okay.

17:44.310 --> 17:46.380
Yuuichi, you can come in.

17:51.420 --> 17:53.150
You're an idiot.

17:55.590 --> 17:58.360
I didn't think you'd come in through the balcony.

17:59.060 --> 18:01.260
You knew that I was coming?

18:02.660 --> 18:08.870
I thought you would be screaming and crying at the door and get chased away by Mama.

18:11.470 --> 18:13.000
Hey, Rika.

18:13.970 --> 18:15.240
What?

18:16.440 --> 18:18.240
Can I be at your side?

18:20.180 --> 18:22.750
Can I always... always...

18:22.750 --> 18:24.080
be at your side?

18:24.620 --> 18:26.780
We can't be together for long though.

18:28.550 --> 18:30.920
But it won't be that short either.

18:32.060 --> 18:33.260
I understand.

18:35.030 --> 18:39.730
You'll have to give up everything for me...

18:40.570 --> 18:42.270
I understand that too.

18:44.540 --> 18:47.040
Are you really fine with that?

18:47.640 --> 18:49.410
This is something I've decided.

18:49.410 --> 18:51.140
So you can't oppose it.

18:52.140 --> 18:53.710
You are an idiot.

18:59.720 --> 19:02.120
We'll be together forever, Rika.

19:04.790 --> 19:07.290
Together forever...

19:09.660 --> 19:12.260
How long did that girl live?

19:12.700 --> 19:16.570
After the first attack, she stabilized for three years.

19:17.500 --> 19:19.200
When the second attack happened,

19:19.200 --> 19:22.210
her heart was as weak as it could get,
not being able to undergo a further operation.

19:23.940 --> 19:26.840
Even like that, she held on for a year.

19:26.840 --> 19:27.910
I see.

19:28.980 --> 19:33.020
He gave up the promotion and chose to stay by her side.

19:34.450 --> 19:36.820
And now he has nothing.

19:37.790 --> 19:40.560
Ezaki will be facing a similar road.

19:41.360 --> 19:43.330
Rika's defects can never be completely cured.

19:43.900 --> 19:45.530
No matter how much he sacrifices...

19:45.530 --> 19:47.800
One day, he'll lose everything.

19:49.570 --> 19:51.000
So what?

19:53.400 --> 19:55.770
For Yuuichi, it may be like that,

19:55.770 --> 19:57.740
but for Rika, it's completely different.

19:59.380 --> 20:00.610
What do you mean?

20:00.950 --> 20:04.450
When Rika is with Yuuichi, she's always laughing, right?

20:04.450 --> 20:07.790
Before, she never laughed at all.

20:07.790 --> 20:09.990
But now she's laughing so happily.

20:11.890 --> 20:14.260
Maybe one day she'll die.

20:14.860 --> 20:15.890
But...

20:17.060 --> 20:21.330
Dying without any happiness and dying with a smile...

20:21.330 --> 20:23.230
Which way is more fulfilling?

20:25.300 --> 20:28.210
For a girl, even if it's only for a short time...

20:28.210 --> 20:31.210
No, because it is only for a short time...

20:31.480 --> 20:33.210
For them to be happy to their hearts' content,

20:33.510 --> 20:35.950
or be filled with joyous laughter...

20:35.950 --> 20:38.580
If such moments exist, somehow I can accept their fate.

20:39.250 --> 20:40.180
Rika is...

20:40.750 --> 20:42.390
right now very fortunate.

20:44.290 --> 20:46.590
What happens to the people who are left behind?

20:47.130 --> 20:48.590
They have to endure it.

20:50.160 --> 20:51.600
It sounds like it's nothing when you say it.

20:51.830 --> 20:54.100
What's the most important thing?

20:54.530 --> 20:55.970
Your own happiness?

20:55.970 --> 20:58.670
Or the happiness of the person you love the most?

21:00.970 --> 21:02.810
I'm going outside for a smoke.

21:21.430 --> 21:23.730
Men sure are stupid.

21:23.730 --> 21:25.600
Even though they don't realize it,

21:25.600 --> 21:28.130
they already have everything.

21:29.270 --> 21:30.500
At that moment,

21:31.000 --> 21:33.770
a silver, half moon hung in the night sky.

21:35.010 --> 21:37.410
Even though it's not as bright as a full moon,

21:37.980 --> 21:40.110
the world has dissolved into the color of the night.

21:40.610 --> 21:45.080
But it still uses its own light to brighten the world.

21:51.660 --> 22:01.130
nee, yubisaki de anata wo kanjite

21:51.660 --> 22:01.130
Hey, I felt you with my fingers.

22:03.740 --> 22:13.280
nee, anata to miteita kono keshiki

22:03.740 --> 22:13.280
Hey, while seeing this view together.

22:16.780 --> 22:26.590
tsutawaru yasashisa ni mi wo yudanete

22:16.780 --> 22:26.590
And then I committed myself to your kindness.

22:26.590 --> 22:37.940
eien nado nai wakatte ita tsumori dayo

22:26.590 --> 22:37.940
I know nothing lasts forever.

22:41.140 --> 22:47.110
namae wo yobu anata no koe wo

22:41.140 --> 22:53.080
I will keep your voice, which calls my name, in the bottom of my heart,

22:47.110 --> 22:53.080
mune no oku ni shimatte oku kara

22:53.080 --> 22:59.190
hirakareta tobira no mukou gawa de

22:53.080 --> 22:59.190
On the other side of the open door,

23:06.900 --> 23:07.770
Oh?

23:07.770 --> 23:08.800
What is it?

23:10.230 --> 23:11.370
Come over here.

23:12.200 --> 23:13.540
You come over.

23:20.010 --> 23:20.910
Rika,

23:21.310 --> 23:23.510
I'll definitely...

23:24.320 --> 23:25.520
will cherish you...

23:27.990 --> 23:29.290
So...

23:29.290 --> 23:31.420
This is your second time saying it.

23:32.590 --> 23:34.890
You said it when we were here last time too.

23:34.890 --> 23:36.230
I see...

23:42.570 --> 23:43.600
Yuuichi.

23:46.140 --> 23:47.040
Yes...

23:48.070 --> 23:49.210
We'll...

23:49.810 --> 23:51.580
go on like this, hand in hand.
